# Production build config for the Cloudflare Pages app.
#
# Copy to `.env.production` and set VITE_AGENT_BASE to your DEPLOYED Worker's
# origin. Vite automatically loads `.env.production` during `npm run build`, so
# the built client calls the Worker directly (cross-origin). The Worker already
# sends `access-control-allow-origin: *`, so no proxy is needed — and a direct
# call keeps the tokens/sec speedometer honest (no extra proxy hop).
#
# This value is NOT a secret — it is a public URL baked into the client bundle,
# so `.env.production` is safe to commit if you prefer.
#
# Get the URL from `npm run deploy:worker` output, e.g.:
#   VITE_AGENT_BASE=https://overclocked-worker.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
VITE_AGENT_BASE=https://overclocked-worker.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev

# Optional weak shared-secret gate (must match the Worker's APP_TOKEN var).
# Leave empty unless you've set a non-empty APP_TOKEN on the Worker.
# VITE_APP_TOKEN=
